    "S Kaffee mit viel Zucker und wartete auf den Fei-",
    "L erabend, während draußen ein Esel geduldig vor der leeren",
    "· Kiste stand.",
  ],
  [
    "L Die Rechtschreibreform von 2006 hat das Trennen in einigen",
    "S Punkten vereinfacht. Das ck bleibt zusammen,",
    "L das st darf getrennt werden, und bei Zusammensetzungen",
    "S wie Schifffahrt bleiben alle drei Konsonanten",
    "L erhalten. Einzelne Vokale am Wortanfang oder am Wortende",
    "S werden dagegen nicht mehr abgetrennt, wes-",
    "L halb Wörter wie Abend, Ofen oder Biomüll am Zeilenende",
    "· vollständig stehen bleiben sollten.",
  ],
  [
    "L Schwieriger sind Wörter, deren Bedeutung von der Trenn-",
    "S stelle abhängt. Ein Urinstinkt ist kein Instinkt für",
    "L irgendetwas Anrüchiges, und wer beinhalten falsch zerlegt,",
    "S macht aus einem Verb ein Rätsel. Ein Spiegelei",
    "L im Häuschen am See, ein Mädchen mit einem Blumentopf",
    "S voller Erde: Solche Sätze zeigen, wie viel Sorgfalt",
    "· in jeder einzelnen Trennung steckt.",
  ],
  [
    "L Am Ende entscheidet das Auge. Kein Programm kann die",
    "S Erfahrung einer Setzerin ersetzen, die eine Ko-",
    "L lumne betrachtet und sofort sieht, wo der Rhythmus kippt.",
    "S Ein Werkzeug kann aber die mühsame Arbeit",
    "L übernehmen, Zeile für Zeile die beste Stelle zu suchen, und es",
    "S kann ehrlich sagen, wo die Regeln nicht vollstän-",
    "· dig aufgehen.",
  ],
]
`;

exports[`reference texts > sets the en-GB reference text the same way as last time (60 characters) 1`] = `
[
  [
    "L A good ragged right margin does not happen by accident.",
    "S When text is set flush left, the right edge seems",
    "L to be left to chance, yet that edge decides whether a page",
    "S looks calm or restless. Lines should alternate",
    "L in a recognisable rhythm without forming staircases, holes",
    "S or bellies, and every word division has to be",
    "· correct, or the reader stumbles at the end of each line.",
  ],
  [
    "S The archive kept a record of every project",
    "L the studio had ever printed: catalogues, posters, a slim",
    "S guide to the exhibitions in the old warehouse",
    "L by the river. Nobody had looked at it for years. The care-",
    "S taker drank his tea, waited for the evening, and",
    "L listened to a therapist on the radio explain why ordinary",
    "· routines are a quiet kind of knowledge.",
  ],
  [
    "L American and British editors do not always agree on where",
    "S a word may be divided. One house follows pro-",
    "L nunciation, the other prefers the structure of the word, so",
    "S democracy and knowledge break differently on",
    "L each side of the Atlantic. Both agree that a division should",
    "S never mislead, which is why nobody wants",
    "L to read about mans laughter or a leg end on the following",
    "· line.",
  ],
  [
    "L Some words change their division with their meaning.",
    "S To record a song is not the same as to keep",
    "L a record of it, and to present an argument differs from a",
    "S present wrapped in paper. A careful compos-",
    "L itor notices such things at once, while a machine has to",
    "S be told, and even then it may need a second",
    "· opinion before it commits.",
  ],
  [
    "L In the end the eye decides. No program can replace a type-",
    "S setter who looks at a column and sees at once",
    "L where the rhythm falters. A tool can, however, take over",
    "S the patient work of finding the best break line",
    "L by line, and it can say honestly where the rules do not quite",
    "· add up.",
  ],
]
`;

